*Infinite [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 133.33~266.67 seconds<sup>4,000f~8,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
At this point, most if not all of your [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] should be at level 10. The stage can still be beaten with lower levels, but it will be much harder. Having at least half of the [[Treasure]]s in your current chapter is also highly recommended, especially the [[Legendary Cat Sword]] and [[Legendary Cat Shield]].

When the battle begins, Jackie Peng and Hippoe will appear, let them get near your base. Meanwhile, upgrade your [[Worker Cat]]. When they come close enough, send out some meatshields, [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] and [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cats]]. But don't overdo it, because you don't want to hit the enemy base just yet.

All the money you get from killing the enemies should help you max out the Worker Cat. Once maxed, just wait for your wallet to fill up. By the time the Gory comes, your wallet should be completely full. That's when you can spawn all of your Normal Cats at once. Then focus on spawning meatshields, Sexy Legs Cats, UFO Cats, [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cats]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cats]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]].

After a short time, Le'boin will join the party, which shouldn't be too hard considering that the Mythical Titan Cats will do their job. Kang Roo will also appear, but he shouldn't be much of a threat. However, if Kang Roo is tearing through your army, you should either spam meatshields or save up money for more heavy hitters. At this point, the enemy base should have already taken some good damage. If you are fast enough, you won't even need to encounter Teacher Bear and One Horn. If you do have to face them, your cats will most likely not be able to kill them in time before they respawn, so make sure to destroy the base before they start to spawn.

You can also instead spam [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] and [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Frog Ninja Cats]]. The Frog Ninja Cats will kill the first lot of enemies, and then once they get to the enemy base, there should only be three Jackie Pengs. The Jackie Pengs can't advance through the Wall Cats in time while the Frog Ninja Cats destroy the enemy base.

